enadid"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/osman-yusuf-kenadid.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Osman Yusuf Kenadid</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Osman Yusuf Kenadid was a Somali poet and scholar, a son of Sultan Yusuf Ali Kenadid of Hobyo.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/osmania-university"><span class="enc-name">Osmania University</span><span class="enc-type">Institution</span><span class="enc-snip">Osmania University is a public university in Hyderabad, India, founded in 1918 by Mir Osman Ali Khan, the last Nizam of Hyderabad.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/osmanya"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/osmanya.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Osmanya</span><span class="enc-type">Term</span><span class="enc-snip">Osmanya is an alphabet for the Somali language created around 1920 by Osman Yusuf Kenadid, son of the sultan of Hobyo.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/osnabruck"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/osnabruck.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Osnabrück</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Osnabrück is a city in Lower Saxony, Germany, on the Hase river.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/osogbo"><span class="enc-name">Osogbo</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Osogbo is a city in south-western Nigeria and the capital of Osun State.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/osorkon-i"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/osorkon-i.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Osorkon I</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Osorkon I was the second king of the Twenty-second Dynasty of Egypt, son of Shoshenq