e">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Osred I (c. 697–716) became king of Northumbria as a boy of about eight on the death of his father Aldfrith in 705, after a disputed succession.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ossetia"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/ossetia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ossetia</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Ossetia is a region of the central Caucasus inhabited by the Ossetians, an Iranian-speaking people descended from the medieval Alans.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ossetians"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/ossetians.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ossetians</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Ossetians are an Iranian-speaking people of the central Caucasus, living in North Ossetia–Alania in Russia and in South Ossetia.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/ossonoba"><span class="enc-name">Ossonoba</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Ossonoba was a town of Roman Lusitania on the Algarve coast of southern Portugal, at or near the site of modern Faro.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/ossossane"><span class="enc-name">Ossossane</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Ossossane was a large Wendat (Huron) village in Huronia, in what is now Simcoe County, Ontario, the main town of the Bear nation.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ostasio-iii-da-polenta"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/ostasio-iii-da-polenta.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ostasio III da Polenta</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ostasio III da Polenta was the last lord of Ravenna from the Da Polenta fa